ab  to gain the function of infecting humans  no rand paul did not describe this  research accurately  the starting virus the one that was  actually engineered it was not just an  animal virus  it was a virus that was already well  known to efficiently enter  human cells because its spike proteins  are a perfect match for our human  ace2 receptors so given that  pretty big and important error that rand  paul made  i do think it's it's fair for dr  fauci to have said this senator paul you  do not know what you are talking about  rand paul also claims that this research  counts as gain of function research  according to dr fauci's own definition  and that funding this type of gainer  function research had been banned by the  federal government  when dr fauci's group approved funding  for this chinese research  is that true does this chinese research  count  as the type the specific type of gain of  function research that was actually  banned  in 2014 to 2017 let's take a look  at exactly what was banned in 2014.  this here is the actual document  announcing the ban of gain of function  research  and on page one of this document we have  the definition  new usg funding will not be released for  gain of function research projects  that may be reasonably anticipated to  confer attributes  to influenza mers or sars viruses  such that the virus would have enhanced  pathogenicity  so it makes it so it gets people more  sick and or  transmissibility in mammals via the  respiratory route  the research funding pause would not  apply to characterization  or testing of naturally occurring  influenza mers  and sars viruses unless the tests are  reasonably anticipated to increase  transmissibility and or pathogenicity  technically speaking that research that  was done in china does not qualify  as this type of gain of function  research and the reason for that is that  the with one virus first of all it's not  a sars virus it's a  sars like virus so it's  technically it's not covered in this ban  furthermore that virus was already able  to get inside of human cells  so by removing its spike protein which  is the tool that it used to get inside  of human cells  and replacing that spike protein with a  different spike protein that we found  from other viruses  that does not enhance its ability to get  inside of human cells it could already  do it  perfectly what we did is we were just  testing to see if these other spiked  proteins  could also let it get inside of human  cells this research  really wasn't any more dangerous  than just working with a virus that  could infect human cells  it the gain of function that was given  here  was not a gain of function that  increased the danger  of this virus in fact the genes that  make this virus  replicate slowly inside of a cell once  it gets inside those were not messed  with at all  so this was not  gain of function research according to  this definition so rand paul is wrong  here  again that said this  this doesn't count as gain of function  research really  on because of a technicality  i do think it's very important that  people understand  the research we're doing in laboratories  is dangerous  and it's important that we  we have a discussion about this that we  understand this  as members of the public that we  understand what's happening we  understand what the risks are  what the potential benefits are and i do  believe  that our government officials have done  a really poor job  explaining this to us in a way that the  average person  can understand so i do think that  fauci and crew need to step up their  game in public education  when he got in front of congress and  testified that we have never funded gain  of function research  in wuhan china yes he's technically  correct not  this type specific type of gain of  function research but we have funded  dangerous research in muhan china  and he should have made that clear when  he was  testifying he should have made that  clear and he did